g draw clears cutoutDraw + onCutoutDraft(null,null) but does NOT call any callback to exit drawing mode (design doc line 88 says pointer cancellation clears both draft AND chosen shape); destroy() clears cutoutDraw + draft callback; TAP_MAX_DISTANCE=8 screen px; MIN_ITEM_SCALE=0.01; edge gesture keeps opposite edge fixed (verified math).\n- src/editor/state.ts lines 150-429: validators confirmed strict as summarized; createSessionFromDocument counts counters by kind (cutout counter = number of cutout layers, so migrated \"Cut Out 1\" yields counter 1, next name suffix 2).\n- src/styles.css lines 675-744: `.more-sheet .more-form{min-height:0; overflow-y:auto; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); ...}` at line 695; `.compact-more-sheet .more-form{flex:0 0 auto; overflow-y:visible}` at line 714 — same specificity, compact later in file wins for elements with both classes. `.more-sheet{overflow:hidden}`.\n- src/editor/ui/sheets.tsx lines 385-634: isDecalSolid helper exists (line 393); fieldValue/commitField cutout branches (left/up/turn/size; size = round avg of w+h, commit scales both by ratio, guards value>0); MoreSheet visibleFields for cutout = [left,up,turn,size] only; compact flag line 539; Escape listener; Done button aria-label Done.\n- src/editor/ui/workspace.tsx (445 lines, full): overlay draw effect verified (dataset cleanup, draft ellipse/rect stroke, selection strokeEllipse vs strokePolygon, data attributes); Escape listener only when drawingCutoutShape !== null; setCutoutDraft(null) effect when drawingCutoutShape null; gesture controller created once with propsRef indirection; itemFootprint returns null for hidden/non-decal solids; cutoutFootprint uses footprintGeometry with source {width: rect.width, height: rect.height}, scaleX/Y=1, handleBounds inset 16.\n\n## Provisional findings so far (not yet final)\n- Candidate MINOR: gestures.ts onPointerCancel (line ~762) discards in-progress draft but leaves drawing mode active, whereas design doc says pointer cancellation clears draft AND chosen shape. No data loss; child can re-drag or tap Cancel.\n- Candidate MINOR/unverified: drawing mode can coexist with an open sheet only if some path opens a sheet without clearing drawingCutoutShape — all identified paths (onToolbar, onTabChange, resetSession) clear it; needs confirmation of onOpen/handleFile/resetSession coverage in designer-app.tsx (not yet read in full).\n- Verified OK: handle-first hit ordering preserves ellipse handle dragging; wheel shape-aware; migration strict; CSS specificity ordering correct; compact More fields = 4 inputs 2-col grid.\n\nStill to do: read designer-app.tsx reset paths + archive.ts 141-300 + compose.ts erase area + SheetBackdrop; optionally run typecheck/unit tests; write final findings + verdict."}]}
