utput used WITHOUT re-validation, but verified safe (see state.ts below). Asset manifest/bytes/sha256/dimension checks unchanged and strict.\n\n## state.ts (lines 150-374 read)\n- isValidPaintLayerShape (155-180) rejects kind !== solid|raster, so isValidProjectDocumentV1 (297+, tail at 300-321 uses isValidPaintLayerShape for ALL layers) can never contain cutouts → migrateProjectDocumentV1 (323-325) `{...document, schemaVersion: 3, layers/assets sliced}` is SAFE (v1 predates cutouts).\n- CUTOUT_KEYS_V2 (no shape), CUTOUT_KEYS_V3 (with shape), CUTOUT_RECT_KEYS exact sets; hasValidCutoutBase requires finite positive width/height, finite centers/rotation; isValidCutoutLayerV2Shape/isValidCutoutLayerShape enforce hasOnlyKeys + shape ∈ {rectangle, ellipse} for v3. migrateProjectDocumentV2 (353-362): cutouts → {...layer, shape:\"rectangle\", rect:{...rect}}, preserves names/geometry. hasValidDocumentHeader(value, 1|2|3) checks format/schemaVersion/name/garmentType.\n\n## compose.ts (348 lines, relevant sections read)\n- validateDocument (53-97): cutout branch rejects shape not in {rectangle, ellipse} or non-finite/non-positive rect geometry (`layer ${index} (${layer.name}) has invalid cutout geometry`).\n- eraseCutout (292-310): save → destination-out → globalAlpha 1 → translate(centerX, centerY) → rotate(rotationDeg) → ellipse: ctx.ellipse(0, 0, width/2, height/2, 0, 0, 2π) + fill; rectangle: fillRect(-w/2, -h/2, w, h); restore. Geometry matches gestures pointInFootprint ellipse math and workspace overlay drawing exactly.\n- composeProject (312-348): validateDocument first; paints all visible non-cutout layers, then second loop erases all visible cutouts — single erase path shared by editor 2D, export, save validation, and 3D preview.\n\n## editor-screen.tsx (353 lines, read full)\n- Single AddSheet Cut Out entry: `onCutout={props.onChooseCutoutShape}` (line 301). CutoutShapeSheet rendered for sheet===\"cutout-shape\" (305-307) with onChoose=onStartCutout, onCancel=onCloseSheet. Selection label (179-182): ellipse → \"Oval Cut Out\" else \"Rectangle Cut Out\". More button in selection-bar; Workspace receives drawingCutoutShape/onCreateCutout/onCancelCutout.\n\n## sheets.tsx (lines 1-135 read)\n- SheetBackdrop: role=\"dialog\" aria-modal aria-label, backdrop-click → onDismiss (target===currentTarget only).\n- AddSheet: big-choice buttons Choose Picture/Choose Color/Cut Out/optional Generate + sheet-cancel.\n- CutoutShapeSheet (103-134): SheetBackdrop label \"Cut Out Shape\" onDismiss=onCancel sheetClass=\"cutout-shape-sheet\"; h2 title; two big-choice shape-choice buttons with IconRectangle/IconOval + visible labels \"Rectangle\"/\"Oval\" and aria-labels; sheet-cancel Cancel; window Escape listener → onCancel.\n\n## gestures.ts (lines 670-794 read)\n- pointerdown during draw starts cutoutDraw with shape from options.cutoutShape() and calls onCutoutDraft with tap rect immediately (line 676). onPointerMove/Up abort draft if drawingCutout() false or cutoutShape() !== cutoutDraw.shape (694-698, 723-727). onPointerUp commit: computes tap/rect, clears cutoutDraw, onCutoutDraft(null,null), onCreateCutout(rect, shape) (720-739).\n- **KEY FINDING**: onPointerCancel (762-781) cutout branch: `cutoutDraw = null; options.onCutoutDraft?.(null, null); return;` — does NOT exit drawing mode (no callback clears drawingCutoutShape), contradicting design doc line 88 (\"...or pointer cancellation clears both the draft and chosen shape\") and plan line 235 (\"pointer cancellation clear chosen shape/draft\"). Recoverable: visible Cancel button exists at workspace.tsx:424 (`aria-label=\"Cancel Cut Out\"`), Escape also works; no data loss/stale state. Fix: add options.onCancelCutout?.() in that branch (wire to props.onCancelCutout via propsRef in workspace.tsx controller options).\n\n## Design/plan wording confirmed\n- design doc line 88: \"Starting a different tool, changing tabs, opening/starting a project, Cancel, Escape, or pointer cancellation clears both the draft and chosen shape. Pointer-up creates exactly one layer and one undo entry.\" Line 20: shape choice closes sheet, activates 2D editor, shows existing draw instruction and Cancel action. Line 95: 44 CSS-px targets. Lines 105-106: pointer cancellation restores pre-gesture geometry; cancelling never dirties project.\n- plan line 235: \"Cancel, backdrop, Escape, tab/tool changes, New/Open, and pointer cancellation clear chosen shape/draft\"; line 256: \"Every existing transient reset path must set the chosen shape to null.\"\n\n## Verified OK (no findings)\nAll reset paths clear drawing state; single Cut Out entry; shape sheet accessible (dialog, Escape, backdrop, Cancel); erase/hit-test/overlay geometry consistent; v1 migration safe (no cutouts in v1); v2→v3 preserves names/geometry; strict key-set validation everywhere; compose single erase path for 2D/export/save/3D; cap checked at sheet-open and create; stale-gesture guards on move/up/create; second pointerdown during draw ignored; package.json scripts: typecheck=tsc --noEmit, lint=eslint ., test:unit=vitest --project unit, test:browser, test:e2e=playwright.\n\n## Final finding for report (one total)\nMINOR — src/editor/ui/gestures.ts:762-767 — onPointerCancel discards the in-progress cutout draft but leaves drawing mode active, violating design doc line 88 / plan line 235 which require pointer cancellation to also clear the chosen shape; concrete scenario: system pointercancel (palm rejection/incoming call) leaves a child silently stuck in drawing mode with no visible draft until they tap Cancel or draw again. Fix: expose a cancel callback in the controller options (e.g. options.onCancelCutout), invoke it in the cutout branch of onPointerCancel, and wire it in workspace.tsx to props.onCancelCutout via the propsRef indirection.\n\nVerdict decided: APPROVE WITH CHANGES (single MINOR spec deviation; everything else verified; note gap that test suites could not be re-run in this read-only environment)."}],"topic":"Ellipse review: final verification"}
